WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.819
Open Call Notes on the intended incident and enter
the update.

00:00:03.999 --> 00:00:07.881
In this training exercise, the server connection is
unavailable.

00:00:08.061 --> 00:00:11.560
Choose Add Note once so you can check what happened
to that update.

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:13.843
The note appears with the Queued badge.

00:00:14.023 --> 00:00:17.820
Omni IC saved it on this device and still needs to
send it.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.165
A search team or wildland crew can use this badge to
tell which changes are waiting for a connection.

00:00:24.485 --> 00:00:28.197
Open Storage and sync from the waiting changes
indicator.

00:00:28.377 --> 00:00:32.665
Under Pending changes, this example shows one item
for the call note.

00:00:32.845 --> 00:00:36.045
Retrying means the app is attempting to send it
again.

00:00:36.225 --> 00:00:40.385
Once you have a connection, Retry is available for an
individual item.

00:00:40.705 --> 00:00:43.799
After the connection returns, check the same outbox.

00:00:43.979 --> 00:00:49.611
In this example, it cleared automatically and the
waiting, failed and stuck counts are all zero.

00:00:49.931 --> 00:00:53.259
Reopen Call Notes and confirm the update is still
there.

00:00:53.439 --> 00:00:55.956
We also checked the note in a separate session.

00:00:56.136 --> 00:01:02.003
That gives a crew handoff or community outreach team
a way to confirm the update reached the server.
